# Line-ending policy.
#
# This file matters here more than in most repositories because two vendored
# third-party trees are committed (`MIDAS-API-main/`, `MIDAS-API-NX-SDK-main/`).
# With `core.autocrlf=true` and no attributes file, Git normalises their LF
# endings on commit and rewrites them to CRLF on checkout — so the working copy
# silently stops matching upstream, which defeats the point of vendoring a
# snapshot. Those two trees are therefore pinned to `-text`: byte-identical, no
# conversion, no warnings.

# Default: normalise text files to LF in the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# --- vendored upstream snapshots: never touch a byte -----------------------
MIDAS-API-main/** -text
MIDAS-API-NX-SDK-main/** -text

# --- binary ----------------------------------------------------------------
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.whl binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.exe binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
*.xlsm binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mgb binary

# --- SQL is text; the schema is diffed on every review ---------------------
*.sql text eol=lf

# --- generated JSON is diffed, so keep it LF and let it merge --------------
*.json text eol=lf

# --- Git's own machinery ---------------------------------------------------
.gitattributes text
.gitignore text
*.md text eol=lf
